Package: luna
Type: Package
Title: Analysis of Sleep Signal Data with 'Luna'
Version: 1.8.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Shaun", "Purcell", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "smpurcell@bwh.harvard.edu"),
    person("John", "Muschelli", role = "ctb",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-6469-1750"))
    )
Description: An R interface to the 'Luna' toolset for the analysis of sleep
    and other physiological signal data (EDF/EDF+). It mirrors the API of
    the 'lunapi' Python package <https://pypi.org/project/lunapi/>, which
    it uses via 'reticulate': projects and sample lists, instances with
    their signals and annotations, 'Luna' commands with output as typed
    data frames, and plots. Requires no compilation: the 'Luna' engine is
    provided by the 'lunapi' wheel, which is installed on first use.
License: GPL (>= 3)
URL: https://zzz.nyspi.org/luna/, https://github.com/remnrem/lunaR
BugReports: https://github.com/remnrem/lunaR/issues
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    R6,
    reticulate (>= 1.41),
    graphics,
    grDevices,
    stats,
    utils
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    withr
SystemRequirements: Python (>= 3.9, < 3.15) with the 'lunapi' Python
    package (>= 1.7.1, < 2), provisioned automatically by 'reticulate'.
    'lunapi' provides binary wheels for macOS (x86_64, arm64), Linux
    x86_64 (glibc >= 2.28) and Windows x86_64.
Config/testthat/edition: 3
